/target
/local
# The client bundle `just build-web` writes into the package whose build
# script embeds it; `crates/sprawling/Cargo.toml` lists it for the
# crates.io archive by name, since cargo leaves ignored files out.
/crates/sprawling/web-dist/
/.lake
# `just mutants` writes its report and the previous run's beside the
# workspace root.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/
# `mlugg/setup-zig` points Zig's global cache at the workspace root, and
# the leaf's build fills it with the system libraries it resolves. Build
# output, like `target/`, and the same row `walk::SKIP_DIRS` carries so no
# gate reads it (tools/xtask/Spec.lean §8).
/.zig-cache/
# svelte-check's generated transpiled project (its --tsgo lane and editor
# tooling write it); it is build output, and ESLint's flat config lints
# dot directories unless they are ignored (client/eslint.config.ts).
.svelte-check/

# Working records never ship. To a contributor and to a model they are
# noise; to an attacker they are intelligence — they name a machine, a
# toolchain, an account, a schedule, and the words a decision arrived in.
# `local/` is where they live, and `xtask release` refuses any published
# document that sends a reader there.
#
# The three city names are root-anchored: a city writes its own Roadmap,
# Memo and Handoff, and `crates/city/templates/` ships the empty shells it
# writes them from. Only a copy left at the root of this repository is a mistake.
/Roadmap.md
/Memo.md
/Handoff.md

# These have no product meaning anywhere in the tree.
NOTES.md
TODO.md
SCRATCH.md
WORKLOG.md
JOURNAL.md
PROGRESS.md
*.session.md
*.handoff.md

# The workflow runner's own directory: per-agent worktrees and run state,
# one machine's scratch, never part of the product.
/.pi/
